# Code owners — who must approve a change before it can merge.
#
# This file is the enforcement half of CONTRIBUTING.md. "Require review from Code Owners" in the
# branch ruleset reads it, so a pull request touching any path below cannot merge until an owner
# has approved it. Without this file that rule matches nothing and silently passes.
#
# Order matters: the LAST matching pattern wins, so the broad rule comes first.

# Everything, by default.
*                           @Alayra-Systems-Pvt-Limited/maintainers

# ── Paths where a bad change is worst ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# CI and release automation. A pull request that edits a workflow is a pull request asking for the
# permissions that workflow holds — this repository publishes to npm via OIDC and to two container
# registries. Treat any change here as a credential change, because that is what it is.
/.github/                   @Alayra-Systems-Pvt-Limited/maintainers

# Secrets at rest, and the boundary that decides who may touch them.
/src/lib/crypto.ts          @Alayra-Systems-Pvt-Limited/maintainers
/src/lib/backup/            @Alayra-Systems-Pvt-Limited/maintainers
/src/middleware/            @Alayra-Systems-Pvt-Limited/maintainers
/src/routes/admin/          @Alayra-Systems-Pvt-Limited/maintainers
/src/services/auth*         @Alayra-Systems-Pvt-Limited/maintainers
/src/services/ssrf*         @Alayra-Systems-Pvt-Limited/maintainers

# The database shape. A migration is the one change that cannot be rolled back by reverting a commit.
/prisma/                    @Alayra-Systems-Pvt-Limited/maintainers

# Licensing and project governance.
/LICENSE                    @Alayra-Systems-Pvt-Limited/maintainers
/SECURITY.md                @Alayra-Systems-Pvt-Limited/maintainers
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md         @Alayra-Systems-Pvt-Limited/maintainers
/CONTRIBUTING.md            @Alayra-Systems-Pvt-Limited/maintainers
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @Alayra-Systems-Pvt-Limited/maintainers
